  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "When Tai Bai Yun Sheng’s immortal aperture forms, a tributary of the river of time flows in the darkness and the time flow rises steadily. Blessed land grade tracks how large a tributary it draws: small blessed lands draw a small tributary and form over ten beads of immortal essence; medium grade draws a slightly bigger tributary and forms over twenty; high grade draws a large tributary, forms over thirty, and can leave spare heaven and earth qi that refine a mortal Gu into an Immortal Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        609
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tai_bai_yun_sheng",
        "sys_blessed_lands_and_grotto_heavens",
        "sys_mortal_gu",
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The change in time flow is the main reason an immortal aperture becomes a small world and attracts a tributary. Spring Autumn Cicada feeds on the water of the river of time, so sitting near that source lets it drink heavily and recover faster.",
      "chapters": [
        631
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_spring_autumn_cicada"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan’s strength path blessed land pulls in an invisible tributary that supports the small world’s normal operations, with outside-to-inside time flow at one to sixteen and twenty-two green grape immortal essence beads, matching medium grade. The same grade ladder is restated when he inspects that aperture.",
      "chapters": [
        633
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A ten extreme physique that succeeds at immortal ascension forms a super grade blessed land larger than high grade. Its tributary of the river of time is gigantic, and green grape immortal essence surpasses fifty beads.",
      "chapters": [
        690
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "super-grade-draw",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan teaches that Hu Immortal blessed land has basic time path dao marks, so it can draw in a tributary of the river of time, let time exist inside the blessed land, and let time flow.",
      "chapters": [
        821
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "dao-marks-of-time",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_hu_immortal_blessed_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Tributaries of the River of Time are commonly seen yet rare. Every Gu Immortal’s immortal aperture has one so time can flow in that world, but tributaries in the five regions and two heavens are few and much larger; super forces fight for them, and lone immortals hide them. Feng Jiu Ge finds such a tributary under a sand whirlpool, with wild day Gu, month Gu, year Gu, ripples of time, and year beasts. Aperture tributaries are too small to enter the River of Time; only a regional tributary with nearly the same time flow as the River of Time can serve as an entrance.",
      "chapters": [
        1400
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "regional-entrances",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_feng_jiu_ge",
        "gu_day_gu",
        "gu_month_gu",
        "gu_year_gu",
        "sys_aperture",
        "loc_river_of_time"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The sand-whirlpool tributary is a secret Shadow Sect cultivation resource on their map. Tributaries in the five regions are Fang Yuan’s planned entrances to the River of Time. After one is lost eliminating pursuers, Shadow Sect still has five or six left, with only one final Western Desert tributary under their control. Eastern Sea’s located tributary has already been taken by Miao Ming Shen.",
      "chapters": [
        1403
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "shadow-sect-resource",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_shadow_sect",
        "reg_western_desert",
        "reg_eastern_sea",
        "char_miao_ming_shen"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In the sovereign immortal aperture, Years Pass Like Days expands the tributary of the River of Time rapidly so the river water flows faster, raising an already high rate of time and making calamities and tribulations occur more rapidly.",
      "chapters": [
        1482
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "sovereign-aperture-flow",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "move_years_pass_like_days"
      ]
    }
  ],
